# The byte state a fresh `Zeroed` token sets: the token's meaning, with
# the premise (made after the bytes' last write) Verus does not check.
axiom_zeroed_bytes	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
# Exposed provenance: challoc's memory comes from `mmap` as integers, so a
# cast of an address in it is valid wherever the first pointer was.
axiom_cast	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
